1. PURPOSE

Alexander4 is developing Vigo, a distributed state enforcement engine.
This agreement grants Partner an unlimited-node, perpetual license to
the Software in exchange for active participation in testing, feedback,
and a public partner announcement during a one-year participation
period. This agreement is limited to no more than five (5) design
partners at any time, at Alexander4's sole discretion.

2. DEFINITIONS

All capitalized terms not defined herein have the meanings given in the
Vigo LICENSE file. "Software" means the Vigo server, agent, CLI, and
all associated code, documentation, and configuration files.

3. LICENSE GRANT

Subject to the terms of this agreement and the LICENSE file, Alexander4
grants Partner a non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable
license to use the Software in compiled binary form for Partner's
internal business purposes, with no limit on managed node count.

Upon successful completion of the participation period (Section 5), the
license becomes perpetual. The license is governed by all terms and
restrictions in the LICENSE file, including Use Prohibitions,
Restrictions, and Security and Access Warning.

4. REVOCATION

Alexander4 may revoke this license for cause, including but not limited
to:

a) Violation of the Use Prohibitions in the LICENSE file.
b) Breach of confidentiality obligations (Section 8).
c) Breach of the Restrictions in the LICENSE file.
d) Use of the Software to provide a hosted, managed, or SaaS offering.
e) Assignment or transfer in violation of Section 17.
f) Failure to run the latest released version of the Software after
   written notice and a fourteen (14) day cure period.
g) Any conduct that, in Alexander4's reasonable judgment, poses a
   material risk to Alexander4's reputation, intellectual property, or
   business interests.

Upon revocation, Partner must cease all active use of the Software
within thirty (30) days. Partner may retain copies solely for regulatory
record-keeping and disaster recovery archives, provided such copies are
not actively used.

5. PARTICIPATION PERIOD

The participation period begins on the effective date and lasts one (1)
year. During the participation period, Partner agrees to:

a) ENVIRONMENT — Deploy the Software in a production environment
   managing real workloads, or a staging environment that mirrors
   production in scale and configuration. The environment must manage
   a minimum of twenty-five (25) nodes. The specific environment is
   described in the Access Scope addendum.

b) FEEDBACK — Provide feedback including bug reports, usability
   observations, and operational experience. Partner shall respond to
   reasonable requests for feedback from Alexander4 within fourteen (14)
   days. Either party may request a meeting at any time.

c) VERSION CURRENCY — Run the latest released version of the Software
   at all times. Upgrades must be applied within seven (7) days of
   release.

d) ACCESS — Provide access to Partner's environment as agreed upon
   separately in writing. Access scope varies by partner and is
   negotiated individually.

e) COMPLIANCE VERIFICATION — Permit Alexander4 to verify compliance
   with the obligations in this section, including confirming the
   deployed version and environment scale. Alexander4 may request
   evidence of compliance at reasonable intervals, and Partner shall
   respond within fourteen (14) days.

If Partner fails to meet these obligations, Alexander4 may terminate
this agreement under Section 10.

6. PARTNER ANNOUNCEMENT

Within thirty (30) days of the effective date, Partner shall publish a
public announcement of the design partnership. The form and placement of
the announcement shall be agreed upon by both parties and must be
reasonably prominent — not buried in a location unlikely to be seen.

Alexander4 shall publish a corresponding announcement within the same
timeframe.

Upon termination or revocation, both parties shall remove all
partnership announcements within thirty (30) days.

7. MARKETING RIGHTS

Partner grants Alexander4 the right to use Partner's company name,
logo, and results (including metrics such as convergence times, drift
reduction, and compliance scores) in Alexander4's marketing materials,
website, case studies, and sales collateral. Specific metrics and data
points require Partner's prior written approval before publication;
once approved, such materials are not considered Confidential
Information under Section 8.

Alexander4's right to use Partner's name, logo, and any previously
approved materials for the period in which the partnership was active
is irrevocable and survives termination of this agreement. Partner may
request removal of materials referencing the partnership as ongoing or
current, in which case Alexander4 shall update such materials within
thirty (30) days.

8. MUTUAL CONFIDENTIALITY

Each party ("Receiving Party") agrees to protect the other party's
("Disclosing Party") Confidential Information with the same degree of
care it uses to protect its own confidential information, but no less
than reasonable care.

Alexander4's Confidential Information includes the Software's source
code, documentation marked as proprietary, unpublished features,
roadmap, pricing, and any trade secrets disclosed during the
partnership.

Partner's Confidential Information includes hostnames, IP addresses,
network topology, system traits, compliance reports, configuration
details, and any other infrastructure data disclosed to or observed by
Alexander4 during the partnership.

Confidential Information does not include information that: (a) is or
becomes publicly available without breach of this agreement; (b) was
known to the Receiving Party before disclosure; (c) is independently
developed without use of Confidential Information; (d) is received
from a third party without restriction; or (e) has been approved for
publication under Section 7.

Either party may disclose Confidential Information to the extent
required by law, regulation, or court order, provided that the
disclosing party gives the other party prompt written notice (where
legally permitted) and reasonable opportunity to seek a protective
order before disclosure.

This confidentiality obligation survives termination of this agreement
for a period of three (3) years.

9. FEEDBACK AND INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY

Partner may submit feature requests, suggestions, bug reports, and
ideas ("Feedback") at any time. All Feedback becomes the sole and
exclusive property of Alexander4 upon submission, with no obligation
of compensation, attribution, or confidentiality. Partner hereby
assigns to Alexander4 all right, title, and interest in any Feedback,
including any intellectual property rights therein.

Alexander4 retains sole discretion over whether to implement any
Feedback, for any reason or no reason. The license granted herein is
not contingent on any Feedback being accepted or delivered.

10. TERMINATION

Either party may terminate this agreement with thirty (30) days written
notice.

Alexander4 may terminate immediately if Partner:

a) Violates the Use Prohibitions in the LICENSE file.
b) Breaches the confidentiality obligations in Section 8.
c) Fails to meet the participation obligations in Section 5 after
   written notice and a thirty (30) day cure period.

If this agreement is terminated before the completion of the
participation period — whether by Partner's voluntary termination,
Alexander4's termination for cause, or mutual agreement — the license
does not become perpetual and Partner must cease use of the Software
within thirty (30) days.

Alexander4's right to revoke under Section 4 is unaffected by
completion of the participation period.

11. SUPPORT

Support is provided on a best-effort basis during the active
development cycle. Alexander4 does not guarantee response times, bug-fix
timelines, or availability for this agreement. If Partner requires
guaranteed support, a separate paid support agreement may be negotiated.

12. NO COMPETING TOOLS RESTRICTION

Partner is free to use any other configuration management, automation,
or infrastructure tools alongside the Software. There is no exclusivity
requirement.

13. NO WARRANTY

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS
OR IMPLIED. THE FULL NO WARRANTY AND LIMITATION OF LIABILITY TERMS IN
THE LICENSE FILE APPLY TO THIS AGREEMENT IN THEIR ENTIRETY. PARTNER
ACKNOWLEDGES THAT THE SOFTWARE IS IN ACTIVE DEVELOPMENT AND MAY CONTAIN
BUGS, INCOMPLETE FEATURES, OR BREAKING CHANGES.

14. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, ALEXANDER4'S TOTAL
AGGREGATE LIABILITY UNDER THIS AGREEMENT SHALL NOT EXCEED FIFTY U.S.
DOLLARS ($50). THIS LIMITATION APPLIES REGARDLESS OF THE THEORY OF
LIABILITY. THE FULL LIMITATION OF LIABILITY TERMS IN THE LICENSE FILE
APPLY.

15. GOVERNING LAW

This agreement is governed by and construed in accordance with the laws
of the State of Oregon, United States, without regard to its conflict of
laws principles. The Governing Law, Dispute Resolution, and Severability
provisions of the LICENSE file are incorporated herein by reference.

16. ENTIRE AGREEMENT

This agreement, together with the LICENSE file, COMMERCIAL-TERMS.md,
and any access scope addendum, constitutes the entire agreement between
the parties with respect to the design partnership. This agreement
supersedes any prior discussions, understandings, or representations
regarding the partnership. In the event of a conflict between this
agreement and the LICENSE file, the LICENSE file governs except where
this agreement explicitly grants broader rights (e.g., unlimited node
count).

17. ASSIGNMENT

This agreement may not be assigned, transferred, or delegated by
Partner, whether voluntarily, by operation of law, or by merger,
acquisition, change of control, or reorganization, without prior
written consent from Alexander4. Any attempted assignment without
consent is void. Alexander4 may assign this agreement freely.

A "change of control" means any transaction or series of related
transactions resulting in a change of more than fifty percent (50%)
of the voting power or equity ownership of Partner. Upon a change of
control, Partner must notify Alexander4 in writing within thirty (30)
days. Alexander4 may, at its sole discretion, consent to continuation,
renegotiate terms, or terminate this agreement.

18. NOTICES

All notices required or permitted under this agreement shall be in
writing and shall be deemed delivered when:

a) Sent by email to the contact address specified in this agreement,
   with confirmation of receipt (read receipt or written
   acknowledgment); or
b) Sent by certified mail, return receipt requested, to the mailing
   address of the receiving party.

Either party may update its notice address by providing written notice
to the other party.
